fix(forms): stop edit screens submitting empty fields and zeroing balances

A subagent review found the account and transaction edit forms were always blank.

Cause: the entity loads asynchronously, but the form state was a plain
remember { mutableStateOf(account?.name.orEmpty()) }. On first composition the
account is null, so every field initialised empty and never re-initialised when
the row arrived — there was no key. Worse for accounts: the blank balance parsed
to 0.0 and the PUT submitted it, silently wiping the account's balance.

- Both forms key their state on the loaded entity id, so fields populate when the
  row lands.
- The account form now refuses an empty balance in edit mode rather than coercing
  it to zero.
- Secondary defect from the same review: the transaction edit fallback called
  load() with the default filter (limit 20), so any transaction outside the
  newest 20 could never be found and the form stayed blank regardless.
